Detached external gradients undefined; non-detached max alpha partial=1.6000000000002002.
\image(figures/wgan_interpolation.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The5 points are supplied interpolation values. A detached leaf still receives an actual input derivative; it separates that derivative from external data and G paths.)
\alttext(Five evenly spaced points form a horizontal real/fake interpolation segment, accompanied by a checked detach versus no-detach gradient control.)

> Clip biases as well as kernels, at an explicit point in the schedule

The original clipping trial constrains every critic tensor to[-.01,.01] once
after initialization and again after every critic optimizer step. It does not
clip after G. The next hand check supplies magnitude.2 to all four critic tensors,
including the two bias vectors, and calls `ClipWassersteinCritic` once. That
function validates every candidate before any write and preserves names/order/
gradient flags. Weight clipping alone does not certify a1-Lipschitz critic.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/wgan_clipping.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore c(5503);
  n::models::WassersteinCritic(c, n::zeros({1, 2}));
  std::vector<double> index, before, after;
  int                 k = 0;
  for (auto& name : c.names()) {
    c.set(name, n::full(c.at(name).shape(), (++k % 2) ? -.2 : .2));
    index.push_back(k);
    before.push_back(n::max(n::abs(c.at(name))).item());
  }
  n::models::ClipWassersteinCritic(c);
  for (auto& name : c.names()) {
    after.push_back(n::max(n::abs(c.at(name))).item());
    if (after.back() != double(.01f))
      throw std::runtime_error("all critic tensors clipped");
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(0, .3)
      .lines(index, before, "Supplied magnitude.2", {220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .points(index, before, "", {220, 38, 38}, 4)
      .lines(index, after, "Explicit clip to.01", {37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .points(index, after, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .x_label("1 hidden/W;2 hidden/b;3 output/W;4 output/b")
      .y_label("Maximum absolute value in each tensor")
      .title("Every critic leaf is constrained, including biases")
      .save_svg("build/wgan_clipping.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/wgan_clipping.svg)
// result_end
\caption(These magnitudes are supplied for the toy. The fitted clipping trial begins from the source Glorot initialization and zero biases before its first clip.)
\alttext(All four supplied critic tensor magnitudes change from.2 to.01, including both bias vectors.)

> Generate three independent ordered ring pools through the native API

`GaussianRingPoints` cycles component i%8 around radius2 and adds independent
Gaussian deviation.08 using local source-compatible midpoint/Box-Muller streams.
The fitting pool has400 rows(seed5507), validation128(seed5519), and test128
(seed5521). This is a synthetic teaching distribution, not an external dataset
or labelled fitting task. The two trials reuse these exact pools and the same
batch order5557. The final16-row batch is retained:13 batches per epoch and39
G steps over three fixed epochs. Three critic steps per batch give117 C steps.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/wgan_pools.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto p      = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.x_limits(-3, 3).y_limits(-3, 3);
  for (auto [count, seed, name, color] :
       std::vector<std::tuple<int, int, std::string, dm::graphics::RGB>>{
           {400, 5507, "Fit400", {37, 99, 235}},
           {128, 5519, "Validation128", {16, 145, 74}},
           {128, 5521, "Test128", {220, 38, 38}}}) {
    auto x = n::models::GaussianRingPoints(count, seed);
    p.points(
        n::select(x, 1, 0).to_vector<double>(),
        n::select(x, 1, 1).to_vector<double>(),
        name,
        color,
        2.5);
  }
  p.x_label("Coordinate1")
      .y_label("Coordinate2")
      .title("Independent synthetic pools on the same eight-component ring")
      .save_svg("build/wgan_pools.svg");
}
```
