> Inspect every held-out interpolation norm, not just its average penalty

These are all128 input-Jacobian norms at the source held-out interpolations,
sorted separately within each trial for a distribution view. Sorting preserves
every norm but does not pair row identities across curves. The horizontal target1
is a reference, not an achieved constraint. The1e-12 guard keeps the norm finite
at a zero Jacobian. It does not force the Jacobian itself away from zero.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/wgan_norms.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
