> Verify the actual input derivative against a separately derived Jacobian

For C(x)=tanh(xW1+b1)w2+b2, the row Jacobian is
((1-tanh(xW1+b1)^2)*w2^T)*W1^T. The native output retains both this analytic
calculation and the actual autograd input derivative. Both final checkpoints give
source maximum disagreement0 across both coordinates of all128 interpolations.
The following comparison plots every coordinate for both trials. Agreement of
this diagnostic does not by itself validate the penalty parameter derivative;
that requires the separate second-order checks and component comparison below.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/wgan_jacobians.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace n = dm::nn;
using A     = std::map<std::string, n::Tensor>;
A Read(const std::string& file) {
  A a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz(file))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  return a;
}
int main() {
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.x_limits(-1.2, 1.2).y_limits(-1.2, 2.);
  p.lines({-1., 1.}, {-1., 1.}, "Identity", {120, 120, 120}, 1);
  for (auto [variant, color] : std::vector<std::pair<std::string, dm::graphics::RGB>>{
           {"clipped", {37, 99, 235}}, {"gradient_penalty", {220, 38, 38}}}) {
    auto out = Read("build/wasserstein_gan/" + variant + "/probe-final-output.npz");
    auto x   = out.at("input_gradient").to_vector<double>(),
         y   = out.at("symbolic_input_gradient").to_vector<double>();
    double error =
        n::max(n::abs(out.at("input_gradient") - out.at("symbolic_input_gradient"))).item();
    if (error != 0)
      throw std::runtime_error("source exact input Jacobian diagnostic");
    p.points(x, y, variant, color, 3);
    std::print(
        "{}: {} input-gradient coordinates, maximum disagreement{}.\n", variant, x.size(), error);
  }
  p.x_label("Analytic input-gradient coordinate")
      .y_label("Actual autograd input-gradient coordinate")
      .title("Two Jacobian calculations agree at all held-out points")
      .save_svg("build/wgan_jacobians.svg");
}
