// result_end
\caption(Vector norms describe scale; the recorded full-coordinate sum and independent derivatives check the actual gradient relation. They are not estimates of sample quality.)
\alttext(Three first-batch critic parameter-gradient norms compare the base game,weighted penalty and full objective, with all65 coordinates saved.)

> Noise sensitivity is an active-path check, not a distribution guarantee

For the final penalty-trial generator, compare all128 original test codes, a
changed bank(seed5573), and128 zero codes at the same weights. The zero bank
repeats one point; changed codes yield different coordinates. These
checks establish a noise-only, nonconstant generation path. They do not establish
mode coverage. Both short fitted distributions visibly miss the ring despite
exact restore, single/batch parity and immutable inference checks.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/wgan_noise_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace n = dm::nn;
using A     = std::map<std::string, n::Tensor>;
A Read(const std::string& file) {
  A a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz(file))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  return a;
}
int main() {
  auto original = Read("build/wasserstein_gan/gradient_penalty/probe-final-output.npz").at("fake");
  auto controls = Read("build/wasserstein_gan/gradient_penalty/probe-noise-controls.npz");
  auto p        = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.x_limits(-3, 3).y_limits(-3, 3);
  for (auto [name, value, color] :
       std::vector<std::tuple<std::string, n::Tensor, dm::graphics::RGB>>{
           {"Original128", original, {37, 99, 235}},
           {"Changed codes128", controls.at("changed"), {220, 38, 38}},
           {"Zero codes128", controls.at("zero"), {16, 145, 74}}})
    p.points(
        n::select(value, 1, 0).to_vector<double>(),
        n::select(value, 1, 1).to_vector<double>(),
        name,
        color,
        3);
  p.x_label("Generated coordinate1")
      .y_label("Generated coordinate2")
      .title("Changing noise changes points without fitting the target ring")
      .save_svg("build/wgan_noise_controls.svg");
}
